{"schema":1,"method":"Geometric interpretations of the named wall sections. Source photographs remain outside the viewer.","sourcesByOwner":{"DEBE00YYaW0000ED":{"name":"Hamberger C&C Großmarkt","sources":["https://www.ks-architekten.de/de/projekte/shopping_handel/hamberger_berlin/","https://www.ks-architekten.de/media/images/projekte/hamberger_berlin/01_Ansicht.jpg","https://www.hamberger-cc.de/agb-berlin"],"note":"Kühnl + Schmidt locate the glazed frontage on the east. The site photograph shows a dark glass wall with slim mullions, an opaque upper fascia and solid concrete side. A broad glazed upper field is drawn only on the two retained eastern faces; pitch and reveal height are approximate. The lower opaque entrance block is left free.","ortho":{"url":"https://gdi.berlin.de/services/wms/truedop_2026?service=WMS&version=1.3.0&request=GetMap&layers=truedop_2026&styles=&crs=EPSG%3A25833&bbox=386858.48%2C5821596.92%2C387113.29%2C5821786.06&width=509&height=378&format=image%2Fjpeg","sha256":"984c9b221988e4308c98b66510c98ed55dfd4db3a277c10cfcff7fa3f0316d54"}},"DEBE11AL2eF0006s":{"name":"Panattoni Park Berlin Zentrum, Halle E (City Dock M21)","sources":["https://panattonieurope.com/de-de/immobilien-suchen/city-dock-berlin-zentrum","https://panattonieurope.com/media/1197/download/City-Dock-M21.pdf?v=1","https://www.berlin.de/ba-lichtenberg/auf-einen-blick/wirtschaft/wirtschaftsbericht_2023.pdf"],"note":"The project plan identifies the long central 15,140 m² logistics hall, separate from the smaller two-storey City Dock units. On the current orthophoto trailers are docked along the eastern side. Individual door positions follow these trailer centre lines, with representational widths/heights. The photographs and plan show white panels and narrow blue upper trim.","ortho":{"url":"https://gdi.berlin.de/services/wms/truedop_2026?service=WMS&version=1.3.0&request=GetMap&layers=truedop_2026&styles=&crs=EPSG%3A25833&bbox=399679.45%2C5822852.37%2C399817.92%2C5823102.31&width=276&height=499&format=image%2Fjpeg","sha256":"35e7a37cc9b6ec2629d965366bb0b4082a0b20f45080c4837dc4a1cb775d51aa"}},"DEBE01YYK0002Mcf":{"name":"Fleischgroßhandel, Berliner Großmarkt","sources":["https://www.berliner-grossmarkt-gmbh.de/fileadmin/user_upload/BGM_Gel%C3%A4ndeplan.pdf","https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/27328106"],"note":"The matching archive facade shows red-brown vertically divided upper cladding and two separated dark loading openings on the northern bay. The occupied truck positions in the 2026 orthophoto confirm the active loading side. Colors are simplified for the viewer; the adjoining Fruchthof entrance is a different building.","ortho":{"url":"https://gdi.berlin.de/services/wms/truedop_2026?service=WMS&version=1.3.0&request=GetMap&layers=truedop_2026&styles=&crs=EPSG%3A25833&bbox=385715.05%2C5821694.54%2C385951.62%2C5821861.25&width=473&height=333&format=image%2Fjpeg","sha256":"d48bd44629a84742cd4d18be024480edd09d39b377a1045e5908e08504da6e62"}},"DEBE09YYO0000Kyh":{"name":"CURVE-Campus, ehemalige Solon-Produktionshalle","sources":["https://www.beos.net/objekte/curve-campus","https://www.beos.net/wp-content/uploads/objekte/161_the_curve/The_Curve_01-1-480x320.jpg"],"note":"The retained polygon is the skylit production hall attached to the office. The garden-facing curved office glass wall is outside this owner. Three lower hall faces have dark cladding above a pale horizontal plinth, measured in wall-registered photographs. The upper unobserved hall volume stays unpainted.","ortho":{"url":"https://gdi.berlin.de/services/wms/truedop_2026?service=WMS&version=1.3.0&request=GetMap&layers=truedop_2026&styles=&crs=EPSG%3A25833&bbox=401018.11%2C5809537.43%2C401187.53%2C5809759.91&width=338&height=444&format=image%2Fjpeg","sha256":"38b2ba430ee64aa9409a312540c5b04511392253ebdcebc4acd62d35747ae846"}},"DEBE09AL1ai000Ck":{"name":"Allianz Campus, Merlitzstraße 8 / Hans-Schmidt-Straße 5","sources":["https://www.hines.com/properties/allianz-berlin","https://www.deutsches-architekturforum.de/thread/4728-wista-wissenschafts-und-wirtschaftsstandort-adlershof/?pageNo=12","https://www.deutsches-architektur-forum.de/pics/backstein/daf/2020/10/wista_allianz_campus04.jpg","https://www.deutsches-architektur-forum.de/pics/backstein/daf/2020/10/wista_allianz_campus05.jpg"],"note":"The 2020 in-use views down Merlitzstraße show four continuous window ribbons above glazed ground level, pale grey metal spandrels and regular narrow mullions. Use the road-facing fingers at Merlitzstraße only. Ground floor is omitted because entrances or bridges obscure several segments; per-bay pitch and vertical proportions are visual estimates.","ortho":{}},"DEBE05YYY0000286":{"name":"Zitadelle Spandau, äußere Kurtinen- und Bastionswände","sources":["https://www.berlin.de/ba-spandau/ueber-den-bezirk/tourismus/sehenswertes/artikel.288536.php","https://www.berlin.de/landesdenkmalamt/archaeologie/bodendenkmale/berliner-bodendenkmale/zitadelle-653195.php","https://altstadtmanagement-spandau.de/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/Teil_A_FEK_Zitadelle_Abschlussbericht.pdf"],"note":"The outlines run along the outer brick curtains and projecting bastions in the surrounding moat. Brick and the upper stone course follow the documented fortification wall. Gatehouse, internal museum buildings and earthworks are separate. The individual brick format is representational.","ortho":{"url":"https://gdi.berlin.de/services/wms/truedop_2026?service=WMS&version=1.3.0&request=GetMap&layers=truedop_2026&styles=&crs=EPSG%3A25833&bbox=378585.46%2C5822510.81%2C379008.84%2C5822926.2&width=846&height=830&format=image%2Fjpeg","sha256":"659825f311024aa51c5b7977232829c11f6fcf94d9318cd708c236189c44e590"}},"DEBE02YY200006gs":{"name":"Gestaffeltes Wohnhochhaus am Platz der Vereinten Nationen","sources":["https://denkmaldatenbank.berlin.de/daobj.php?obj_dok_nr=09085180","https://commons.wikimedia.org/?curid=46662229","https://www.lorch-seidel.de/sites/default/files/pdf/lorch-seidel--e-94--Selected-Works-by-Julius-Weiland--web.pdf"],"note":"Three narrow east-facing archive photographs resolve repeated pairs of recessed openings at the actual observed elevations. The four stepped north/south end panels are predominantly closed. ALKIS records 25 storeys for the complex; that count is not applied to its shorter parts.","ortho":{"url":"https://gdi.berlin.de/services/wms/truedop_2026?service=WMS&version=1.3.0&request=GetMap&layers=truedop_2026&styles=&crs=EPSG%3A25833&bbox=393552.27%2C5820390.76%2C393630.14%2C5820517.82&width=155&height=254&format=image%2Fjpeg","sha256":"3eb39fc7b2db755df31cc479b45234d3971c0a8f16ffebbc352ca7a79c6fb788"}},"OSM-relation-175667":{"name":"Ehemaliges Reichsbahnausbesserungswerk, BAUHAUS Alboinstraße","sources":["https://www.nhp-architekten-ingenieure.de/projekt/raw-tempelhof.html","https://denkmaldatenbank.berlin.de/daobj.php?obj_dok_nr=09066445%2CT","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tempelhof_-_Bauhaus_-_geo.hlipp.de_-_31859.jpg","https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Berlin_Bauhaus_am_S%C3%BCdkreuz.JPG","https://www.openstreetmap.org/relation/175667"],"note":"The street photograph and heritage record locate the retained workshop along Alboinstraße. A higher strip of paired openings, a closer middle row and varied ground-floor openings sit in its light masonry facade. The parking entrance has storey-high openings under brick arches. The modern red steel trademarks are excluded. Wall sections, pitch and heights are representations clipped to the existing 7 m mesh.","ortho":{"url":"https://gdi.berlin.de/services/wms/truedop_2026?service=WMS&version=1.3.0&request=GetMap&layers=truedop_2026&styles=&crs=EPSG%3A25833&bbox=389063.75%2C5814226.97%2C389319.68%2C5814449.33&width=511&height=444&format=image%2Fjpeg","sha256":"a5970880ad87cc3e192c8d82b649a07046067dc20530df7621a118f553da8984"}},"DEBE09YYP0002l69":{"name":"Industriehalle Wilhelminenhofstraße, Oberschöneweide","sources":["https://gdi.berlin.de/services/wfs/alkis","https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/40324429"],"note":"The archive view directly on the 37° facade shows a gabled head with a large gridded opening. Nine tall, closely spaced dark window bays in the lower hall along its right side have visible masonry piers. No rows are extended behind the gable or onto the roof.","ortho":{"url":"https://gdi.berlin.de/services/wms/truedop_2026?service=WMS&version=1.3.0&request=GetMap&layers=truedop_2026&styles=&crs=EPSG%3A25833&bbox=399500.11%2C5813064.95%2C399718.76%2C5813280.73&width=437&height=431&format=image%2Fjpeg","sha256":"8dd5d0d39649b15c1ee1b255aff552558a308356e91084fc9c79c5361dc20c12"}},"DEBE04YY5000041B":{"name":"DRK Kliniken Berlin Westend, Haus 1","sources":["https://www.drk-kliniken-berlin.de/westend","https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/185310340"],"note":"The southwest walls of this hospital building show individually readable light-framed punched openings between exposed brick piers. Upper, middle and lower rows are measured only where the photographed wall is visible. The western return has a different horizontal glazed ribbon. Trees and the neighboring buildings are excluded.","ortho":{"url":"https://gdi.berlin.de/services/wms/truedop_2026?service=WMS&version=1.3.0&request=GetMap&layers=truedop_2026&styles=&crs=EPSG%3A25833&bbox=382983.2%2C5820150.05%2C383151.59%2C5820370.43&width=336&height=440&format=image%2Fjpeg","sha256":"b407d546b7a039e4a007f260513bc8995ac799a2c0bab36b1ee2510d803f5328"}},"DEBE01YYK00043PZ":{"name":"Brunnenstraße 106, Laden- und Parkgebäude","sources":["https://gdi.berlin.de/services/wfs/alkis","https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/28022662"],"note":"The south side is a repeated sequence of pale fins and dark recesses on a parking deck. Its northern elevation has a long metal screen on the mezzanine and a contrasting ground-floor canopy. These are opaque material and support sections; photographs do not establish shop windows behind every fin.","ortho":{"url":"https://gdi.berlin.de/services/wms/truedop_2026?serv